      "text": "block           = the name of the block; an empty name stops the check with the BLOCK-NAME error\n\nblock_lines     = the line spans of the block; there must be one span at least, inside the file    (check_spans)\n\nfor each part, in the order of the text:\n    a part is one line of the flow text \u2014 one left-column name; the line:\n\n        \"spans = the real line span of every def and class\"\n\n    is the part named spans; the text is a list of such parts, in order\n\n    is the part name new?                                            no -> PART-NAME stops\n    do the own lines of the part sit inside the block lines?         no -> PART-BOUNDS stops; a part with outside_within and a note passes\n    is each callee a real block of the file, with its true span?     no -> CALLEE-REAL stops    (check_spans)\n    does each constant keep a name and lines inside the file?        no -> CONST-NAME or CONST-LINES stops\n\nwithin          = the zoom into one part of an older entry\n    do the parent entry and its part exist?                          no -> WITHIN-REAL stops\n    does every line of the new block sit inside the lines of that part?    no -> WITHIN-BOUNDS stops    (part_lines)\n\nthe clean entry returns, ready to append",
